A 50 Hz, 275 kV line of length 400 km has the following parameters:

Resistance, R = 0.035 \(\Omega\)/km; Inductance, L = 1 mH /km; Capacitance, C = 0.01 \(\mu\)F/km;

The line is represented by the nominal-\(\pi\) model. With the magnitudes of the sending end and the receiving end voltages of the line (denoted by V_{S} and V_{R}, respectively) maintained at 275 kV, the phase angle difference (\(\theta\)) between V_{S} and V_{R} required for maximum possible active power to be delivered to the receiving end, in degree is _____________ (Round off to 2 decimal places).

